hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18053","Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah narrated to us, he said: Bahir ibn Sad narrated to me from Khalid ibn Madan from Jubayr ibn Nufayr from Ibn Abi Amirah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim soul whose soul Allah Almighty takes that loves to return to you, though it has the world and what is in it, except the martyr."
"18054","And Ibn Abi Amirah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: To be killed in the path of Allah is dearer to me than that mud-brick and camel-hair be mine."
"18055","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Said ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us from Rabiah ibn Yazid from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amirah al-Azdi from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he mentioned Muawiyah and said: O Allah, make him guiding, guided, and guide by him."
"18056","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Hilal ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, he said: Umar looked at Abu Abd al-Hamid, or Ibn Abd al-Hamid, Abu Awanah doubted, and his name was Muhammad, and a man saying to him: O Muhammad, may Allah do to you and do and do, he said: And he went on reviling him, he said: Then the Commander of the Faithful at that said: O Ibn Zayd, come near to me, he said: Do I not see Muhammad being reviled because of you. No, by Allah, you shall not be called Muhammad as long as I live. So he named him Abd al-Rahman. Then he sent to Banu Talhah to change their family's names, and they were at that time seven, and their chief and eldest was Muhammad. He said: Then Muhammad ibn Talhah said: I adjure you by Allah, O Commander of the Faithful, for by Allah none named me Muhammad, meaning except Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then Umar said: Rise, I have no way to anything that Muhammad named."
